    "user_request_original": "Optimize a 22-layer Ge/ZnS multilayer filter on CaF2 substrate for dual-band transmission. Wavelength bands: transmit 3250-3350 nm and 4200-4300 nm; block 2500-3100 nm and 4450-5000 nm. All 22 layer thicknesses are optimization variables with bounds [80, 400] nm. Initialize thicknesses at quarter-wave values (Ge ~205 nm, ZnS ~375 nm at 3300 nm reference). Use gradient-based and differential evolution optimizers with step size reduced by 50% from standard defaults. Evaluate coherent TMM across 2500-5000 nm spectrum. Score candidates by mean transmittance in passbands and blocking bands. No metal layers. Air incidence, unpolarized light. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 2500-3100 nm, 3250-3350 nm, 4200-4300 nm, 4450-5000 nm. soft objectives: High transmittance in 3.25-3.35 um and 4.20-4.30 um bands; Low transmittance in 2.50-3.10 um and 4.45-5.00 um bands. behaviors to suppress or avoid: High transmittance in 2.50-3.10 um and 4.45-5.00 um bands. manufacturing constraints: Total layer count <= 24; No metal layers; Conventional depositable infrared inorganic dielectric materials only.",
